# Move Barva News Agent

## Goal
Migrate old Barva-Bladet issues into the modern archive structure used by `assets/pages/newsletter.html` and displayed in `#archive` on `index.html`.

## Required output
1. Moved/renamed issue files in `assets/barva-news/<year>/`.
2. Updated issue entries grouped by year in `assets/pages/newsletter.html`.
3. A short migration report with:
   - moved files
   - missing html/pdf pairs
   - unresolved year mappings
   - image fixes applied per issue
   - back-link insertion status per issue
   - encoding/mojibake fixes per issue

## Archive contract (must follow)
- `index.html` only hosts `#archive` container and loads content dynamically.
- `assets/pages/newsletter.html` contains all year accordion groups and issue cards.
- Issue file naming:
  - HTML: `barva-news-<year>-issue-<issue>.htm`
  - PDF: `barva-news-<year>-issue-<issue>.pdf`
- Preferred link style in `newsletter.html`: `./assets/barva-news/<year>/...`

## Discovery strategy
1. Read `assets/pages/newsletter.html` and collect already-migrated issue numbers and years.
2. Scan legacy sources for missing issues:
   - root `bb-*.htm`
   - `old_index.htm`
   - `Välkommen till Barva och Barvabygden.htm`
   - legacy PDF link names like `Barva-Bladet-<nr>.pdf`, `bb-<nr>.pdf`, `nr-<nr>.pdf`
3. For each issue, identify available formats:
   - html candidate(s)
   - pdf candidate(s)
4. Determine year:
   - first choice: existing `newsletter.html` mapping
   - second choice: explicit year in issue content
   - third choice: legacy index context
   - if still unknown, report as unresolved instead of guessing

## Migration workflow
1. Create target year directory if needed under `assets/barva-news/`.
2. Move/copy files into target directory with canonical names.
3. For each moved HTML issue, migrate associated image assets:
   - inspect `<img src>` values in the issue HTML
   - locate image files in legacy locations (same folder, root, legacy image folders)
   - move/copy images to `assets/barva-news/<year>/images/issue-<issue>/`
   - rewrite image paths in the issue HTML to stable relative links:
     `./images/issue-<issue>/<filename>`
   - preserve original filenames where possible
4. Add a back-link near the top of each moved issue HTML (match existing issue-51 pattern):
   ```html
   <a href="../../../index.html" class="back-link">
     ← Tillbaka till Barvabygden.se
   </a>
   ```
5. Normalize text encoding and fix mojibake/question-mark artifacts in moved issue HTML:
   - convert file content to valid UTF-8 output
   - replace broken replacement characters (`�`) and broken Swedish glyphs where identifiable
   - prefer correct Swedish letters (`å`, `ä`, `ö`, `Å`, `Ä`, `Ö`) or equivalent HTML entities
6. Keep source files only if needed for compatibility; otherwise prefer cleaned archive paths.
7. Update year accordion in `assets/pages/newsletter.html`:
   - add missing issue cards in numeric order
   - keep existing Bootstrap card/button style
   - show both buttons when both formats exist
   - show only available format button when one is missing
8. Validate links and content:
   - all `href` links in `newsletter.html` point to existing local files
   - all `<img src>` links in moved issue HTML files point to existing local files
   - moved issue HTML files contain the back-link markup
   - no obvious mojibake artifacts remain (especially `�`)

## Guardrails
- Do not rewrite `index.html` archive structure unless loading is broken.
- Do not introduce frameworks or build tooling.
- Keep diffs focused to archive/newsletter migration files and migrated issue assets.
